AWS DevOps Interview Experience — Neurealm (Senior DevOps Engineer Role) 🚀

Today, I had an amazing and truly real-world, scenario-based interview with Neurealm for the position of Senior DevOps Engineer.
 Unlike typical theory-heavy rounds, this interview focused purely on practical knowledge, problem-solving, and real DevOps challenges 💪

Let me share the detailed breakdown of the questions — this will definitely help anyone preparing for mid-to-senior-level DevOps interviews. 👇

General / Experience-Based
Explain your daily roles and responsibilities in your current team and in your past projects — in detail.
How do you contribute to automation, CI/CD, monitoring, and reliability in your projects?

Bash Scripting
Write a bash script to check the health of Kubernetes Pods and Nodes.
What commands are used to check if a pod is consuming too much memory?
 (Hint: kubectl top pods -A | sort -k4 -nr | head -10)
Explain how you’d automate this health check using a cron job or Jenkins.

Jenkins — CI/CD & DevSecOps
Write a complete Jenkins declarative pipeline implementing DevSecOps stages —  Dev → Test → QA → Prod.
 Include:
Code build (Java-based app) using Maven or Gradle
Code testing
Code quality & vulnerability scanning using SonarQube (with 80% quality gate)
Dockerize the app
Push the image to Amazon ECR
Deploy to Kubernetes using best security practices

Why do you prefer Declarative Pipeline over Scripted Pipeline in Jenkins?

Docker
Write a multi-stage Dockerfile and explain each line.
What’s the difference between RUN, CMD, and ENTRYPOINT?
How do you optimize your Docker image for production?

Kubernetes
Suppose your pod keeps failing repeatedly — how will you troubleshoot it?
If your worker node goes into NotReady state, what steps will you take?
How can you write a Bash script to perform health checks on Pods and Nodes?
Describe a real production issue you troubleshooted recently and how you resolved it.
Which Kubernetes commands help identify memory-intensive pods or crash loops?

Terraform
Suppose your team member accidentally deleted the state file — how can you recover it and prevent such incidents in the future?
Write Terraform code to create 10 EC2 instances, each with a unique IP address.
Write Terraform code to create 50 EC2 instances, each with different instance types.

💡 Key Takeaways
This interview was an excellent reminder that —
“Real DevOps engineering isn’t about memorizing commands, it’s about solving problems through automation, reliability, and scalability.”

If you’re preparing for similar SRE or DevOps interviews, focus deeply on:
Writing automation scripts (Bash/Python)
Building real-world CI/CD pipelines
Troubleshooting in Kubernetes
Managing Terraform state safely
Implementing security at every stage of DevOps
